#ROOM
Vnum     50000
Name     Terran Orbital Academy~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors safe~
Desc     You have arrived at Terran Orbital Academy, a training station in orbit above
Earth. This academy teaches the basic commands needed to survive, travel and
interact with other people in the wider interstellar community. Each
compartment has a specific lesson. Explore the academy in full and read each
room carefully. The student message area is to the west; return here afterward
and continue north when you are ready.

The entrance concourse reflects its builders: bright ceramic panels, brushed
metal ribs and broad observation glass. Through the nearest observation panel
you can see Earth's blue oceans, white cloud bands and the curve of the
atmosphere.

Beyond the station hull, Earth turns slowly below in blue, white and green.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    50001
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    50130
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50001
Name     Human Instruction Spine~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This corridor links the academy's first instructional rooms. The language and
communication lesson is to the west, while practical skill instruction is to
the east. When you have finished with both rooms, return here and continue
north.

The passage is built around bright ceramic panels, brushed metal ribs and
broad observation glass, with clean white daylight-spectrum lighting. Displays
along the wall present Human maps, scientific milestones and civic emblems.

Terran Union academy markings and neutral instructional signage line the compartment.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    50004
Desc      Reading Room
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    50003
Desc      The Laboratory of Skills.
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    50000
Desc      Entrance to Terran Orbital Academy
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    50006
Desc      Abigail Keene's Language Lessons.
~
#ENDEXIT

#MUDPROG
Progtype  leave_prog~
Arglist   100~
Comlist   if isimmort($n)
else
  mpforce $n vis
endif
~
#ENDPROG

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50002
Name     Human Navigation Success Annex~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors~
Desc     You completed the navigation exercise successfully. Continue north to return
to the reference room and resume the academy course.

A small window in this quiet annex looks toward Earth, a reminder that the
entire training complex is an orbital station.

The orbital station's clean composite architecture keeps the focus on training and navigation.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    50004
Desc      The Reading Room
~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50003
Name     Human Skills Laboratory~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors safe~
Desc     This is the academy's practical skills laboratory. Type PRACTICE to see the
abilities currently available to you. Your list may include weapon skills,
general skills, languages and other advanced abilities. To improve something,
use PRACTICE <full skill name>.

For example, to practice dual wield, type PRAC DUAL WIELD. Additional
proficiency is gained through training and successful use. Type HELP PRACTICE
or HELP <skill> whenever you need more information.

Human instructors favor a practical combined-arms training tradition. The room
itself is equipped with modular Terran consoles and standardized training
equipment.

Beyond the station hull, Earth turns slowly below in blue, white and green.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    50001
Desc      A Stone Corridor
~
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 50040 1 50003
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50004
Name     Human Reference Archive~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors silence~
Desc     This quiet reference room suppresses most public channels so that students can
read without interruption. Type CHAN for a list of channels. You can disable a
channel with CHAN -<channel>, enable it with CHAN +<channel>, or use CHAN -ALL
and CHAN +ALL to silence or restore them together.

When you are ready, go west for the navigation exercise. Follow the room
descriptions until you find your way back here. If you become lost, the up
route returns you to this room. Once you have completed the exercise, continue
north.

The archive contains Human maps, scientific milestones and civic emblems.
clean white daylight-spectrum lighting keeps the room comfortable for long
periods of study.

Terran Union academy markings and neutral instructional signage line the compartment.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    50014
Desc      A Marble Corridor
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    50001
Desc      A Stone Corridor
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    50007
Desc      Wandering the Academy
~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50005
Name     Human Combat Trials Control~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors safe~
Desc     This chamber is reserved for controlled combat trials. In ordinary play you
will encounter mobiles, often shortened to MOBS. Some may be aggressive and
attack as soon as you enter their location. Defeating opponents can provide
experience and loot.

After a fight, EXAMINE CORPSE and GET ALL CORPSE can be used to inspect and
recover items. CONFIG +AUTOLOOT and related configuration options can automate
parts of this process. REST, SLEEP, WAKE and STAND are useful while recovering
between exercises.

The chamber is arranged around a practical combined-arms training tradition,
with bright ceramic panels, brushed metal ribs and broad observation glass
protecting the rest of the station from the training area.

The orbital station's clean composite architecture keeps the focus on training and navigation.
~
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50006
Name     Human Language and Culture Suite~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors safe~
Desc     This room teaches the language system. Type PRACTICE to see languages
available to you. Your native tongue and the common language are normally
available without additional study. To learn another language, use LANGUAGE
LEARN <language>.

For more information use HELP LANGUAGES, HELP SPEAK and HELP TONGUE. Language
study consumes practice sessions, and capable students generally learn more
efficiently.

The walls carry Human maps, scientific milestones and civic emblems, giving
students examples of how language, history and identity developed among the
Human.

Beyond the station hull, Earth turns slowly below in blue, white and green.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    50001
Desc      A Stone Corridor
~
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 50094 1 50006
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50007
Name     Human Orientation Passage~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This is the beginning of the navigation exercise. Type CONFIG +AUTOEXIT if you
want obvious exits displayed automatically. EXIT lists visible routes, and
LOOK <direction> lets you inspect an adjoining direction before moving.

Your next route is west. Try EXIT and LOOK WEST before moving on. The exercise
uses bright ceramic panels, brushed metal ribs and broad observation glass to
make each section visually distinct without changing the station's underlying
layout.

Terran Union academy markings and neutral instructional signage line the compartment.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    50004
Desc      The Reading Room
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    50009
Desc      Wandering Terran Orbital Academy, it looks safe
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    50004
Desc      Back to the beginning
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    Door~
ExDesc       You see a solid oak door.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50008
Name     Human Combat Practice Bay~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This is a controlled combat practice bay. A restrained training creature is
used here to demonstrate attacking, judging an opponent and withdrawing from a
fight. The CONSIDER command compares your character with a potential opponent;
elsewhere, use CON <MOBNAME> before attacking something unfamiliar.

The bay follows a practical combined-arms training tradition. Heavy barriers
and modular Terran consoles and standardized training equipment keep the
exercise isolated from the inhabited sections of the station.

The orbital station's clean composite architecture keeps the focus on training and navigation.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    50016
Desc      A Dank Pit
~
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 50045 1 50008
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50009
Name     Human Sealed-Access Corridor~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This section teaches doors and less-obvious exits. A closed door may not be
listed among obvious exits until you interact with it. Read the room
description, LOOK <direction>, try moving into a direction, and use OPEN
<direction> or OPEN DOOR when appropriate. HELP OPEN provides more detail.

clean white daylight-spectrum lighting and deliberately repetitive wall panels
make the exercise depend on observation rather than decoration.

Beyond the station hull, Earth turns slowly below in blue, white and green.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    50010
Desc      An Enclosed Room
~
Keywords  door~
Flags     isdoor closed~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    50007
Desc      Wandering the Academy
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
