ExDesc       You see an oak door.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    picture~
ExDesc       This is a picture of fresh cut flowers in a glass vase. It seems to
be hanging here just to cover a huge crack. That crack is so large, you
can probably squeeze through it! Perhaps you should look closer at the
crack. HINT: type CRACK. 
~
#ENDEXDESC

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    crack~
ExDesc       This is a huge CRACK, you could probably squeeze through it. 
~
#ENDEXDESC

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    wall~
ExDesc       This is a picture of fresh cut flowers in a glass vase. It seems to
be hanging here just to cover a huge crack. That crack is so large, you
can probably squeeze through it! Perhaps you should look closer at the
crack. HINT: type CRACK.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50014
Name     Human Readiness Concourse~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This corridor introduces commands used to inspect your character. SCORE shows
core statistics, EQUIPMENT lists worn items, INVENTORY shows carried items,
and LEVEL reports advancement information. Common abbreviations include SC, EQ
and I.

Use HELP <subject> for additional information. The concourse is finished with
bright ceramic panels, brushed metal ribs and broad observation glass, and
clean white daylight-spectrum lighting clearly marks the route toward combat
training.

The orbital station's clean composite architecture keeps the focus on training and navigation.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    50015
Desc      Preparing for combat
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    50004
Desc      The Reading Room
~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50015
Name     Human Combat Briefing Deck~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Combat training is immediately ahead. You can begin an ordinary fight with
KILL <mob>, while many learned skills and abilities can also initiate combat.
Before attacking unfamiliar opponents, use CONSIDER and review the help for
your available abilities.

Remember that aggressive actions against another player can have consequences.
The briefing deck reflects a practical combined-arms training tradition;
modular Terran consoles and standardized training equipment monitors the
practice bay below.

Beyond the station hull, Earth turns slowly below in blue, white and green.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    50017
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    50014
Desc      A Marble Corridor
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction down~
ToRoom    50016
Desc      A Dank Pit
~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50016
Name     Human Withdrawal Training Bay~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors~
Desc     This bay explains ways to leave a dangerous fight. WIMPY can automatically
withdraw you when your hit points fall below a chosen threshold. FLEE attempts
an immediate manual withdrawal. Emergency recall or extraction mechanics may
also exist, but they generally carry a greater cost and should be treated as a
last resort.

The room is intentionally austere, with bright ceramic panels, brushed metal
ribs and broad observation glass and clear route markers designed to make
emergency instructions easy to understand.

Terran Union academy markings and neutral instructional signage line the compartment.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    50008
Desc      A Dank Pit
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    50015
Desc      Preparing for combat
~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50017
Name     Human Recovery Lounge~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors safe~
Desc     Long fights and long journeys require recovery. REST is the safest ordinary
way to recover. SLEEP can recover more deeply but leaves you vulnerable in
unsafe locations. Use WAKE after sleeping and STAND after resting.

Characters can also become hungry or thirsty. Ask the service unit here for
food or a canteen, then use EAT <item> or DRINK <item>. The fountain can also
be used directly or to refill a container.

This is an open, multicultural commons designed for students from every Human
settlement. Beyond the windows lies Earth's blue oceans, white cloud bands and
the curve of the atmosphere.

The orbital station's clean composite architecture keeps the focus on training and navigation.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    50027
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    50015
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 50015 1 50017
Reset M 0 50065 1 50017
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50018
Name     Human Object Interaction Exercise~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors safe~
Desc     Some items that initially appear unimportant can become useful later. Speak
with the student here and pay attention to what they have found.

Containers can hold other objects. Use LOOK IN <container>, GET <item> FROM
<container>, PUT <item> IN <container>, and OPEN <container> when necessary.

Hint: say hello. The exercise occupies a small Human student annex fitted with
modular Terran consoles and standardized training equipment.

Beyond the station hull, Earth turns slowly below in blue, white and green.
~
#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    50022
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 50042 1 50018
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50019
Name     Human Fabrication Loft~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Some objects are obtained by manipulating, combining or crafting other
objects. Your character may eventually learn specialized crafting skills;
other situations are as simple as opening a container or operating a control.

This compact fabrication loft is dense with modular Terran consoles and
standardized training equipment. It mirrors the practical working style found
throughout Terran Orbital Academy.

Terran Union academy markings and neutral instructional signage line the compartment.
~
#EXIT
Direction down~
ToRoom    50022
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 50018 1 50019
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50020
Name     Human Salvage Exercise~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A common way to acquire equipment is to recover it from defeated mobiles.
After defeating the training unit here, use EXAMINE CORPSE to inspect what it
carried and GET ALL FROM CORPSE to recover the contents. Configuration options
can automate looting or currency collection.

The salvage exercise takes place in a reinforced work cell equipped with
modular Terran consoles and standardized training equipment and arranged
according to a practical combined-arms training tradition.

The orbital station's clean composite architecture keeps the focus on training and navigation.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    50022
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 50060 1 50020
  Reset E 1 50001 1 8
  Reset E 1 50002 1 13
  Reset G 1 50004 1
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50021
Name     Human Academy Supply Exchange~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors safe~
Desc     Shops are useful for acquiring equipment and selling items you no longer need.
LIST shows a merchant's stock, BUY <object> purchases something, SELL <object>
offers an item for sale, and VALUE <object> asks what the merchant will pay.

The backpack is particularly useful because it can hold spare equipment. This
supply exchange is decorated with Human maps, scientific milestones and civic
emblems and uses modular Terran consoles and standardized training equipment
for inventory and transaction handling.

Beyond the station hull, Earth turns slowly below in blue, white and green.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    50022
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 50070 1 50021
  Reset G 1 50017 1
  Reset G 1 50011 1
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50022
Name     Human Equipment Acquisition Lab~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Finding better equipment is an important part of progression. Some methods
become available only after learning the appropriate skills, including SEARCH
and DIG. Other methods may carry legal or social consequences.

The rooms east, west, above and below demonstrate different ways to obtain
useful items. Explore all four, then continue north.

This equipment lab uses bright ceramic panels, brushed metal ribs and broad
observation glass; lockers and work surfaces are sized and arranged for Human
trainees.

Terran Union academy markings and neutral instructional signage line the compartment.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    50023
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    50020
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
